    {
      "id": "4rFT2pcAsuWeO7_nArsTy",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 361,
      "y": 679.46875,
      "width": 1534.7388916015625,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2M",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2142184952,
      "version": 1229,
      "versionNonce": 129070840,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785773560871,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Entities\n1. Atm : Responsibility-> Atm coordinates the interaction between user, hardware components and banking servic to complete a transaction\n2. User : Responsibility -> the user is responsible for initiating ATM operations by providing inputs such as card insertion, PIN entry, transaction selection\n3. Card : Responsibility -> the card provides account identification information like number, expiry, bank\n4. Card Reader : Responsibility -> To read card information\n5. Display : Responsibility -> TO present info to user and prompt user\n6. Keypad : Responsiblity -> To read user input\n7. Cash dispenser: Responsibility -> To dispense cash to user\n8. Bank account : Responsibility -> To store responsible to store account information like balance, status, type, transaction history\n9. Bank service : Responsibility -> Gateway to provide banking operations to the ATM like auth, account access, balance updates and transaction processing\n10. Transaction: \n11. \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Entities\n1. Atm : Responsibility-> Atm coordinates the interaction between user, hardware components and banking servic to complete a transaction\n2. User : Responsibility -> the user is responsible for initiating ATM operations by providing inputs such as card insertion, PIN entry, transaction selection\n3. Card : Responsibility -> the card provides account identification information like number, expiry, bank\n4. Card Reader : Responsibility -> To read card information\n5. Display : Responsibility -> TO present info to user and prompt user\n6. Keypad : Responsiblity -> To read user input\n7. Cash dispenser: Responsibility -> To dispense cash to user\n8. Bank account : Responsibility -> To store responsible to store account information like balance, status, type, transaction history\n9. Bank service : Responsibility -> Gateway to provide banking operations to the ATM like auth, account access, balance updates and transaction processing\n10. Transaction: \n11. \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
